  "body": "Continue the exact F15 LegalIR decoder with a bounded modality/conditions readout experiment. Six selected tensors contain 325 active scalars; actor and presence parameters stay frozen. After 32 updates, complete training IR remains 154/168 on both greedy and joint routes, so scientific acceptance, the parent-ablation signal and default promotion remain false.\n\nAdd the decoder, detached contract tests, complete comparison report and compact public evidence. Preserve the existing grouped and latent decoders. The report links the diagnostic weights and full evidence at an immutable Hugging Face revision, with forced download verification; no active latent, statutory-semantic, broader logic-family, Lake-build or portable numerical-reload qualification is claimed.\n\nValidation: detached decoder and runner contracts passed; the guarded 32-update run completed; separately authored counts agree across 60 panels, 54 scored sets and 36 comparator/scope groups. Recorded arithmetic covers 384 CE rows, 384 modality CE calculations and 2,304 KL components, with the unverified numerical scope stated explicitly. Exact staged-tree preservation is reviewed separately from model authorship.\n\nUpstream integration preserves main `d0d44b3e0f7c2ba804b0d9115f7a1efd2ad926c3`, including the four new paired-census migration files and all prior tree entries. The interrupted first Hub request is retained; a read-only reconciliation proved its 18 payload files absent before a separately qualified 42-chunk resume.\n\nVerified diagnostic archive: https://huggingface.co/Publicus/legal-ir-autoencoder/tree/c9cce4586dd96518088662fb12831173e98e36cc/releases/20261015-modality-conditions-retention-v1 (395 files, 105,151,374 bytes). Independent raw download completion review is included in the evidence capsule.\n",
